10.5 lf no appeal is received within ten (10) calendar days after the date of the ECMAdministrator's executive determination, then the ECM Administrator's executivedetermination shall be final and the El Paso County Attomey's Office may proceed withlitigation to seek remedies pursuant to subsection l0.l of this Ordinance.
10.6 lfthe ECM Administrator receives atimely appeal ofhis or her executive determination asset forth in Section l0 of this Ordinance, then the ECM Administrator shall place the matteron the Board of County Commissioner's next available hearing agenda which meets therequirements of section 10.7 below.
10.8 At the hearing, the Owner shall have the opportunity to present evidence and testimony toshow cause why further enforcement action should not be taken. The Board of CountyCommissioners shall consider all such evidence and lestimony, along with anypresentation, evidence, or testimony offered by the Department of Public Works or otherEl Paso County staff, in reaching its decision to affirm or overtum the decision to issue theexecutive determination.
10.9 At the conclusion ofthe appeal hearing, the Board of County Commissionen may decideto overtum the decision to issue the executive determination or may affirm the decisionand instruct the ECM Administrator to proceed with one or more of the enforcementmechanisms provided in subsection 10.1 ofthis Ordinance.
Section 11: Criminal Prosecution.
I1.3 Any person who violates this Ordinance commits a civil infraction, and, upon convictionthereof, shall be punished by a fine ofup to one thousand dollars ($1,000) for each separateviolation.
ll.4 The penalty assessment procedure provided in C.R.S. $ 16-2-201 shall be followed inenforcing this Ordinance.
I1.5 Al[ fines and forfeitures collected by the court for the violation ofthis Ordinance shall bepaid to the E[ Paso County Treasurer within thirty (30) days of receipt and shall bedeposited into the General Fund of El Paso County.
17
10.7 The Owner shall be notified ofthe date, time, and place ofthe hearing via first class mailto the Owner's mailing address as listed in the records of the El Paso County Assessor'sOffice no less than five (5) calendar days prior to the hearing.
1l.t After receiving Board approval at a public hearing, the ECM Administrator may initiatethe criminal prosecution ofviolations ofthis Ordinance in the county court.
ll.2 The ECM Administrator shall have the authority to issue citations or summonses andcomplaints for the purpose ofenforcing this Ordinance.

